<title>BRAZIL: Brazil net dollar inflows $28.5 mln June 6.</title>
<headline>Brazil net dollar inflows $28.5 mln June 6.</headline>
<dateline>SAO PAULO 1997-06-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>Preliminary figures for Brazil's commercial and financial foreign exchange contracts showed a $28.5 million surplus on June 6 in the commercial forex market, according to Central Bank data suplied to banks.</p>
<p>The Central Bank issued the following breakdown.</p>
<p>DOLLAR FLOWS ON JUNE 6</p>
<p>Exports: $194 million</p>
<p>Imports: $244.4 million</p>
<p>Finanancial buy: $433.1 million</p>
<p>Financial sell: $354.2 million</p>
<p>Net surplus: $28.5 million</p>
<p>JUNE DOLLAR FLOWS UP DATE</p>
<p>Exports: $1.176 billion</p>
<p>Imports: $1.347 billion</p>
<p>Financial buy: $1.959 billion</p>
<p>Financial sell: $1.778 billion</p>
<p>Net surplus: $10 million</p>
<p>Note: the figures were rounded off.</p>
<p>((--Alexandre Caverni, Sao Paulo Newsroon, 55 11 2485418))</p>
